{
  "slug": "web-vitals-auditor",
  "name": "Web Vitals Auditor",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Run Lighthouse audits, diagnose Core Web Vitals regressions, and audit bundles, images, and fonts for performance wins.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **6 skills**, **2 agents**, **3 commands** and **2 hooks**.\n\n- **Skills** (6): `budget-generate` (Generate a performance-budget.json file for Lighthouse CI with reasonable defaults), `bundle-analyze` (Analyze a Webpack, Vite, or Rollup build output for duplicated dependencies, unexpectedly large packages (lodash, moment, polyfills), and…), `font-audit` (Detect font-loading issues), `image-audit` (Scan HTML, JSX, TSX, and Vue files for unoptimized images), `lighthouse-audit` (Run Lighthouse against a URL in both desktop and mobile form factors and summarize Core Web Vitals), `vitals-diagnose` (Interpret a Lighthouse JSON result and prioritize concrete fixes)\n- **Agents** (2): `perf-forensics` (Use when a web page is slow, a Core Web Vital has regressed, or a Lighthouse score has…), `vitals-interpreter` (Use when a Lighthouse JSON report has been produced and the user wants it read and summarized)\n- **Commands** (3): `doctor` (Check the local performance-audit toolchain), `full-audit` (Run the full Web Vitals audit pass in one command), `serve-audit` (Serve a static build output on a local port, run Lighthouse against it for both desktop and mobile,…)\n- **Hooks** (2): `SessionStart`, `PostToolUse`\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install web-vitals-auditor@claude-community` from `mohitkale/web-vitals-auditor`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude"
  ],
  "pluginType": "package",
